A very weird thing happened with my 10th level monk. He got bit a
jackalwere and got transformed. He prayed, and turned back into human.
Later he was trapped in a narrow space with lots of monsters coming his
way -- the "one man holding narrow passage against a zoo" situation. In
preparation for battle he put on two UNKNOWN uncursed rings -- I
figured: "I know they are not cursed, so can't be anything bad, and may
do some good." As the monk was putting on the second ring, I got "you
have a sad feeling, but it passes" message. Well, halfway through
battle my monk is a jackalwere with 12 hp again! And no way out! I
summoned tame jackals to keep the monsters busy and tried to think what
may have happened. Could one of the rings be a Polymorph? If so, I will
revert to human if I can hold out a few hundred turns... dot... dot...
dot... dot... until a dwarf zombie (IIRC) got in and started wailing on
him. Down to 8 hp... 6... 5... I am about to die! ...and all of a
sudden he is human monk again with FULL hit points!

I immediately took off both rings, made a short work of dwarf zombie,
and took care of what was left of the zoo. But now I wonder? Was it a
ring? And will he turn into a jackalwere again at an inopportune moment?



